course: dictionary
lesson: 530
title: Astronomy: the science of space
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Astronomy is a long word, but its context gives you the meaning. «Astronomy is the science of space» tells you straight away that it is a science about space, not a story or a game.
explain: The sentence «And you can enjoy the stories while knowing the science» sets astronomy against fun things like reading your horoscope. The clue is «still know which is astronomy»: astronomy is the real science, and the others are for fun.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Ella joined an astronomy club» fits if astronomy means the study of stars and planets. «Ella joined a science club about space» also makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Astronomy is the science that studies stars, planets, moons, comets, galaxies and everything else in space.
fact: Astronomers use telescopes and space probes to study space.
fact: In history, astronomy helped sailors find their way and helped people make calendars.
fact: Astrology is a belief about stars and personality, not a science, and tests have not shown it predicts anything.
fact: Useful phrases: study astronomy, an astronomy club, amateur astronomy (astronomy done for enjoyment, not as a job).
exercise: Which word names the science of space? | Horoscope | Shooting star | Astrology | *Astronomy
exercise: Dan joins an astronomy club to look at planets through a telescope. What does a telescope help astronomers do? | *Look at stars and planets | Cook dinner | Keep warm in winter | Bake bread
exercise: «Astronomy is the science of space; astrology is a belief about stars and personality.» Which one is a science? | *Astronomy | Astrology | Horoscopes | Belief in luck
test: «Astronomers use telescopes and space probes.» What do astronomers study? | Animals in the sea | *Stars, planets and other things in space | Cakes and biscuits | Only the weather on Earth
test: In history, astronomy helped sailors. What did it help them do? | *Find their way | Paint their ships | Swim faster | Cook their meals
exam: What is the best meaning of astronomy? | *The science that studies the stars, planets, moons and everything else in space | Making a wish on a shooting star | Reading your horoscope for fun | A belief that stars control your personality
